        "r": 544.2116940000011,
        "b": 687.8032529281769
      },
      "content": "Parameter  is  the  important factor  in  determining  the  characteristics  and  functions  of machine. There  are  ones  for  determining  the  standard  specification  and  selective  one, classification, function, or the capacity or the level of the desired performance. 1) Kinds and major contents a. NC parameter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1245",
      "reading_order": 1596,
      "section": "3-9-4. Parameter",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.37977799999999,
        "t": 679.6950800000001,
        "r": 239.72193000000007,
        "b": 670.823360928177
      },
      "content": "See the NC parameter Table."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1246",
      "reading_order": 1597,
      "section": "3-9-4. Parameter",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.37977799999999,
        "t": 662.655068,
        "r": 478.5656639999997,
        "b": 653.7833489281769
      },
      "content": "For the information, see \"FANUC operating manual\". (2) How to treat the parameter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1247",
      "reading_order": 1598,
      "section": "3-9-4. Parameter",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.37977799999993,
        "t": 645.6751760000001,
        "r": 541.4792399999998,
        "b": 585.803660928177
      },
      "content": "Each parameter (data) has been set at the factory and doesn' t need revise or set, unless otherwise stated (Except for the custom macro, backlash/pitch error compensation areas). In addition, when shipping the machine, the values of NC and PC parameter should be tagged on the machine, so keep and prepare if for further use."
    }
  ],
